WEBVTT

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.420
I can't maintain proper course?

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:15.780
Hell no!

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:28.560
This thing's got more maneuverability 
problems than the Type 97!

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.060
Checkpoint 3 passed. +4.52.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.390
Damn it!

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:37.050
The whole place is packed 
with sleeper drifts?

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:40.940
Set proximity margin and pilot 
safety functions to minimum.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:46.060
Damn it, I'm not letting this shitty 
TSF get the better of me any more!

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:43.030
Hey, are you okay man?

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:45.390
Yeah.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:49.900
Jeez. Turning the pilot safety 
functions off? Are you nuts?

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:51.900
Sure, there's no rule against it, but...

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:55.940
Only got me back .25 seconds though.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:56.730
Ensign Bridges.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:07.980
Is there anything you want to say?

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.140
Sure I do.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:13.520
I thought I'd learned the maneuverability 
traits of Japanese TSFs on the Type 97.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:14.830
But I was wrong.

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:18.860
This thing's an even more 
unbalanced piece of crap.

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:19.640
Seriously?

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:22.120
Indeed.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:25.210
The Shiranui Type-1c, the TSF 
the Type-2 was based off of,

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:29.250
was created with an emphasis on improving 
its combat capability at all costs.

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:33.010
This makes it extremely difficult to pilot.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:38.910
It requires a combination of a 
delicate touch and a bold spirit,

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:42.030
as well as exceptional piloting skills.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:51.780
Perhaps it's too much for an American 
soldier like you after all.

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:54.640
I've only got eighteen 
hours in the thing so far.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.560
32 counting simulations!

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:00.290
By the time it gets into 
trials I'll be ready.

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:02.450
No matter how defective it is.

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:10.890
<b>The Right Stuff</b>

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:26.400
They're just drones! What am I doing?

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.600
Command Post to Argos 1.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.520
We've lost control of Drone 6.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:35.900
It is leaving the area heading to 
point E-92. Recover it immediately.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:37.490
Argos 1, roger.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.040
The Soviets are using E-92.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:43.640
I'd better take care of this 
before they hassle me again.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:48.480
Is that it?

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:54.780
Who's there?

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:01.840
That's...

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:03.540
You again?

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:05.360
That voice... is that?

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:07.590
Retreat.

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:10.300
This is our exercise area.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:11.840
If you approach any further I'll open fire.

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:16.800
Wait. I'm just here to get 
a drone that went offline.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:17.790
Yuuya?

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:21.460
It is you, Yuuya!

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:22.450
Inia?

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:25.540
Yuuya, are you chasing that naughty boy?

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:29.300
Inia. We're doing exercises 
now. That's enough.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.850
But Cryska...

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:33.220
Idar 1, what's wrong?

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:34.730
Get back here and continue your training.

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:37.290
Idar 1, roger.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:37.980
Inia.

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:39.370
Right.

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:41.450
See you later, Yuuya!

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:50.610
Those two are the Scarlet Twins?

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:59.400
What? You didn't know they 
were the Scarlet Twins?

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.710
They're both pretty annoying, right?

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:04.080
But don't touch them.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.830
They're mine.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:12.090
Sure, but make sure that you don't 
end up owing anybody anything else.

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:14.340
Why you?

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:16.530
Wait, VG!

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:16.530
It's the truth!

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:21.250
Wait!

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:22.300
Why you...

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:25.630
What is it that's scaring me?

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:32.840
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:35.950
No matter how good a TSF it is, 
if only veterans can pilot it,

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:39.110
it's nothing more than an expensive coffin!

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:40.120
It's just junk!

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:54.860
What kind of TSF are you planning on making

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:57.260
if you're just going to ignore 
everything the test pilot says?

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.070
Junk, huh?

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:07.430
There's a saying in Japanese: 
A man and his horse are one.

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:10.630
To Eishi in my country, trusting your TSF

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:14.920
and using it to its full potential is 
considered even more important than piloting skill.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:18.270
I was hoping that would 
be true of you as well.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:20.810
A man and his horse are one?

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:22.430
There's nothing wrong with 
that psychological stuff.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:28.010
But just like Eishi on the battlefield, we 
test pilots are risking our lives in reality.

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:30.600
To make those TSFs worth trusting.

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:32.680
That's our pride as test pilots.

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:39.570
I refuse to allow any Eishi 
to die in a TSF I tested.

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:42.680
Even you Japanese.

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:45.690
Is that all you want to say?

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.360
I see.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:52.570
No matter what I say to 
you now it won't matter.

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:56.170
You're running?

00:07:56.170 --> 00:07:58.590
If you're got a problem then out with it!

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:02.480
Then I'll say it.

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:08.070
The XFJ plan does not exist to satisfy 
the pride of its test pilots.

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:11.910
Your demands that this be 
handled in an American fashion

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:13.840
are nothing less than an attempt to 
make the entire project belong to you.

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:16.320
What?

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:19.100
Do not disappoint me further.

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:21.020
You...

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:21.820
Calm down, Yuuya!

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:23.460
Belong to me?

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:27.010
You're the one who's being 
a selfish little girl!

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.660
That woman really pisses me off.

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:47.860
What's Chobi's problem?

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:50.200
Don't talk like it's not your problem.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:52.150
She's mad at what happened to you.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:56.840
It wasn't easy stopping Tarisa 
from running out there

00:08:56.840 --> 00:09:00.040
when you were arguing with the princess.

00:08:58.190 --> 00:09:00.040
Come on! Let me go!

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:03.970
You saw that?

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:05.720
Princess?

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:08.170
Lt. Takamura!

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:11.740
I heard she's from a noble 
family of former samurai.

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:17.010
And a member of the Imperial Royal Guard.

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:20.010
That's one of Japan's elite squads.

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:22.990
So princess isn't just a name for her.

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:26.270
Let's stop talking about that girl.

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:28.490
This is our welcome party for Yuuya.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:31.610
A little late, though.

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:33.090
Guys...

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:33.760
Welcome...

00:09:34.150 --> 00:09:35.270
...to Alaska!

00:09:35.690 --> 00:09:37.060
Cheers!

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.860
Here you go.

00:09:40.860 --> 00:09:42.090
The usual order okay?

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:44.210
Yup. Thanks.

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:45.660
I've been waiting for that.

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:48.110
And those two melons too.

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:50.700
These are off limits.

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:53.350
Oh, who's this monsieur?

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.540
This is a new pilot...

00:09:55.930 --> 00:09:58.240
Hey, he's pretty cute!

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:01.520
Natalie Duclert, from France.

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:02.320
Nice to meet you.

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:04.550
Yuuya Bridges.

00:10:04.550 --> 00:10:05.190
Nice to meet you.

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:10.870
How long are you going 
to put those on my head?

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:13.120
Oh my, you're so violent Tarisa!

00:10:13.470 --> 00:10:17.890
Shut up! Why do you do that 
every single time, Natalie?

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:15.700
Hey, is this okay?

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:17.880
It's nothing new.

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:22.980
It's one of those things where they're each 
drawn to that something they lack in the other.

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:24.670
Where were you looking when you said that?

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:27.210
We're having a welcome party today.

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:28.060
What's your recommendation?

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:30.550
We've got some excellent natural beef.

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:33.180
That sounds good.

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:35.840
I'm sick of artificial meat.

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:38.330
But it's expensive, right?

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:42.330
Hmm... maybe I'll give 
you a discount, Tarisa.

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:45.650
I love you, Natalie!

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:48.180
You and I are best friends!

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:49.850
Okay, I'll take my payment.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:53.670
Wait!

00:10:57.160 --> 00:10:59.140
Chobi, are you...

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:07.370
What is that?

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:08.380
Don't laugh!

00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:10.510
Natalie forced me to wear it.

00:11:10.510 --> 00:11:12.870
Don't make that face, Tarisa.

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:15.020
It looks great on you.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:16.660
R-Really?

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:18.140
Yup.

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:20.500
This'll make a great picture.

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:23.280
Delete that photo!

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:27.330
Wait, Natalie! Wait!

00:11:24.590 --> 00:11:26.660
Oooh, scary!

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:28.170
You're not going to eat?

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:32.020
No, that's not it...

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:34.920
Nothing wrong with this, is there?

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:36.950
VG?

00:11:36.950 --> 00:11:42.930
When she first came here, she never 
smiled. She just frowned all the time.

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:45.160
Part of it was that she didn't want anybody 
to mess with her, probably, but...

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:46.810
You mean Tarisa?

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:47.990
Yeah.

00:11:47.990 --> 00:11:54.980
Most people here are strangers, who've lost 
their homelands to the BETA and ended up here.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:57.700
They never had the luxury to smile.

00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:01.820
Their families, friends, everything 
they had was eaten by the BETA.

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:04.090
And all they had left were themselves...

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:06.220
...and their hatred of the BETA.

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:06.840
Right?

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:11.340
That's why you need to enjoy 
yourself when you get the chance.

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:13.090
Like that.

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:15.340
She's got a tail too.

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:16.750
Cute, huh?

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:20.450
They've fought the BETA on the front lines.

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:26.080
Their burdens are as great, 
or greater than mine.

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:29.710
Is that all you want to say?

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:35.010
Is that true of her, too?

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:44.790
Yuuya Bridges.

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:48.180
The Shiranui Type-2 operates 
on totally different design

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:50.560
and operations principles 
than an American TSF.

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:52.450
And he's steadily mastering 
it in such a short time.

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:58.720
Your talent and potential 
make you an unmatched Eishi.

00:12:59.310 --> 00:13:03.990
But that's not enough.

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:16.420
Resting when you can is part 
of an Eishi's job, right?

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:19.610
Or are you so busy thinking about 
Princess Yui you can't sleep?

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:23.190
Princess Yui? Huh?

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:26.100
Looks like you're getting 
along with her though.

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:29.990
I've known somebody similar for a long time.

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:32.520
I can understand her.

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:35.360
She's a lot like you, Princess Yui.

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:38.490
Bite me. Don't compare me to her.

00:13:38.490 --> 00:13:42.660
The way you don't back off when you should, 
and how you're not honest with yourself.

00:13:42.660 --> 00:13:43.960
She's just like you, right?

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:48.970
It's just like with a TSF.

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:52.050
The question is how well you understand them.

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:54.650
Understand them, huh?

00:13:56.000 --> 00:14:02.140
A TSF designed by a country that lost 
half its territory to the BETA...

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:07.540
Hey, Vincent. What is it about 
this thing I don't understand?

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:13.380
I'll start by saying this: in an 
American TSF you're a top-class Eishi.

00:14:13.380 --> 00:14:14.660
I can testify to that.

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:17.460
But the way you pilot a TSF,

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:20.750
the strategies you use, change totally 
depending on what country made it.

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:27.740
If I tuned it like an American would, 
it'd make it hard for a Japanese to use.

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:30.520
Yup.

00:14:31.190 --> 00:14:35.180
For instance, the maneuverability 
system is totally different.

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:37.760
An American TSF uses brute force.

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:40.460
A Japanese TSF would take advantage of

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:43.800
the aerodynamic properties of its 
knife sheathe or center head mast.

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:50.280
You keep that in mind, and then it's a 
question of how much you can communicate with it.

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:55.290
Is that what she means when she 
says "A man and his horse are one?"

00:14:55.760 --> 00:14:58.100
Couldn't tell you.

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:00.970
Why don't you ask her?

00:15:00.970 --> 00:15:02.530
I guess that's impossible.

00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:05.010
Well, it's like when you're 
in bed with a girl.

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:08.420
Don't just think about yourself. 
Try to satisfy them too.

00:15:08.960 --> 00:15:11.240
Why are you talking about 
women all of a sudden?

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:15.900
You might as well try to ride Princess 
Yui while you're at it, Top Gun.

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:20.470
Why do I have to try and 
seduce that Japanese Doll?

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:24.430
Christ...

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:36.170
I understand the theory.

00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:39.690
All that's left is how well the 94 
Second and I can understand each other.

00:15:40.490 --> 00:15:42.300
I won't try and overpower it.

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:43.420
I'll work with it.

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:46.800
Argos leader to all TSFs.

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:48.790
Initiating case 23.

00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:50.520
Argos 1, roger.

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:51.840
Argos 2, roger.

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:53.490
Argos 3, roger.

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:54.800
Argos 4, roger.

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:56.480
Initiating JIVES.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:03.670
Let's go, 94 Second!

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:17.750
The 94 Second's test parameters 
are far below yesterday.

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:22.100
He never does anything halfway.

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:24.920
Until yesterday he was trying to 
force it to do what he wanted.

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:27.430
And now he's letting it take control?

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:30.930
Crap!

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:37.070
Huh? You done already?

00:16:40.030 --> 00:16:41.570
Shut up, catgirl maid!

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:43.710
Don't say that.

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:49.780
Calm down, guys. I guess that's 
the last one for today...

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:47.110
I guess figuring out the Japanese TSFs

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:49.290
isn't something you can do in a day...

00:16:50.060 --> 00:16:50.900
Huh? What's that?

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:54.950
Something came into the practice 
area without authorization?

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:56.340
Is it a TSF?

00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:59.250
It can't be lost, right?

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:01.010
Argos 1 to Command Post.

00:17:01.010 --> 00:17:02.120
Unknown unit sighted.

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:03.150
Requesting identification.

00:17:03.860 --> 00:17:05.330
Identification in progress.

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:06.870
All units stand by.

00:17:06.870 --> 00:17:07.910
Identification complete.

00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:09.390
This is...

00:17:09.390 --> 00:17:11.260
What are you doing, Lt?

00:17:12.230 --> 00:17:14.460
Command Post, come in!

00:17:14.460 --> 00:17:15.300
Command Post!

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:18.500
What happened?

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:21.350
This isn't funny.

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:23.420
No data match in library.

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:27.200
Attention approaching unknown.

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:28.720
Respond immediately.

00:17:28.720 --> 00:17:30.820
Respond immediately.

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:37.110
Argos 1 to all units.

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:37.790
Prepare for combat.

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:40.780
What's going on?

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:44.780
And what is this awful feeling?

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:48.890
I found the data in your library.

00:17:48.890 --> 00:17:50.550
Only in the 94 Second's?

00:17:52.930 --> 00:17:54.290
The Takemikazuchi?

00:17:56.470 --> 00:18:00.210
Attached to the Imperial Royal Guard?

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:04.970
The Type 00?

00:18:04.970 --> 00:18:05.610
Then is that...

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:08.360
Lt. Takamura?

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:17.810
That sword's for real combat!

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:19.350
Her!

00:18:19.350 --> 00:18:21.930
I guess she wants some attention.

00:18:21.930 --> 00:18:24.820
It's hard to be popular.

00:18:25.970 --> 00:18:30.390
Is that really her? What 
do we do? Do we fight?

00:18:31.190 --> 00:18:33.250
She's mocking you, Argos 1!

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:34.460
Stop it, Tarisa!

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:36.950
If that's how you want it...

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:38.500
Let's do it.

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:44.650
I don't care if you're in the Royal 
Guard or not... get lost, princess!

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:50.840
Get your foot off her!

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:53.760
This is going too far, Lt. Takamura!

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:56.920
Damn it!

00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:00.440
Are you insane?

00:19:00.440 --> 00:19:01.550
Tarisa!

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:07.970
VG! Stella!

00:19:08.920 --> 00:19:10.920
Damn it...

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:13.030
That's you, isn't it Lt. Takamura?

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:19.040
Do you hate me that much?

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:21.550
Come on, Lt.

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:23.290
I'll fight you.

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:33.720
Damn it, damn it all!

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:36.320
Why won't you do what I tell you, 94 Second?

00:19:54.390 --> 00:19:56.430
So you're going to take your time?

00:19:56.430 --> 00:19:58.600
You could take me out in one 
hit any time you wanted!

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:04.250
I can't stop here...

00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:07.170
Without even being able to 
master a Japanese TSF...

00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:09.300
Done in by a Japanese!

00:20:11.880 --> 00:20:12.940
Damn it all!

00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:16.390
I won't lose here!

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:29.080
That movement... did I do that?

00:20:32.220 --> 00:20:35.150
There's a saying in Japanese: 
A man and his horse are one.

00:20:35.860 --> 00:20:40.540
To Eishi in my country, trusting your 
TSF and using it to its full potential

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:43.220
is considered even more 
important than piloting skill.

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:44.770
I see.

00:20:44.770 --> 00:20:46.650
So that's it...

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:51.420
Hey, I'm just like you.

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:54.320
I had my fate messed up by two countries.

00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:58.720
Let's do this together, 94 Second!

00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:19.380
Command Post to all units.

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:20.300
That's enough.

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:22.290
Captain.

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:26.850
White Fang 1, did you 
complete your objective?

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:32.640
Mission complete.

00:21:35.010 --> 00:21:37.050
I can't believe she did that!

00:21:37.550 --> 00:21:40.270
I refuse to accept it!

00:21:40.270 --> 00:21:42.440
She totally got us.

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:45.250
But that was amazing, Yuuya.

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:50.460
You got a solid hit in on Lt. Takamura in 
a TSF you'd barely been able to fly before.

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:53.620
She lost to Yuuya.

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:56.310
She can't be that good.

00:21:56.310 --> 00:21:57.950
Shut up, Churrasco.

00:21:57.950 --> 00:21:58.830
Churrasco?

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:03.750
That means "skewered", 
doesn't it? It's perfect!

00:22:04.070 --> 00:22:07.590
Shut up! Don't give me weird nicknames!

00:22:08.270 --> 00:22:09.690
That feeling...

00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:15.970
If I could master it... you 
and I could be stronger.

00:22:33.370 --> 00:22:35.100
You taught them, didn't you?

00:22:39.430 --> 00:22:40.710
Just like Yuuya...

00:22:43.070 --> 00:22:46.730
And just like Cryska. You're nice.

00:22:48.630 --> 00:22:50.670
Bye bye!

00:22:54.560 --> 00:22:56.030
Cryska?

00:24:07.370 --> 00:24:10.860
If we get there we can take 
shelter from the rain.

00:24:11.640 --> 00:24:14.650
So what's the relationship 
between you and her?

00:24:15.570 --> 00:24:17.500
That man interests me.

00:24:16.970 --> 00:24:24.270
<b>Ultramarine</b>

00:24:19.470 --> 00:24:22.970
Next time on Total Eclipse: Ultramarine
